{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485886-nuwisha-pretending-to-be-a-werewolf","id":1485886,"title":"Nuwisha pretending to be a werewolf?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-05T22:44:05-07:00","id":1485886,"title":"Nuwisha pretending to be a werewolf?","content":"How would you make a nuwisha who is pretending to be a werewolf, and then go about tricking other people into thinking you really are one? I mean, it seems simple enough to say you are a bone gnawer ragabash, and then just pretend like you are one. It would probably trick people for a while. However, I am curious about how to go really deep, to trick everyone. Even other players. Even so they don't notice out of game as well!<br /> <br /> What are some things, that might give you away? Well rage seems like one thing, though ragabash only have one rage, so saying you are 'saving it' seems fairly plausible. Gifts not matching is another thing, though there are some overlap of gifts. That might work at lower levels when no one expects you to know more than a few gifts, but more noticeable later on. I suppose as a ragabash you could get in the habit of telling the dm secret stuff, and play it off as playing tricks and what not, then people might not notice if you secretly active a gift.<br /> <br /> I am just curious on what other people's thoughts are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1926-lilitha","name":"Lilitha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-05T23:01:29-07:00","id":1485887,"title":"","content":"Well check out their breed book. It has a lot of details on how they infiltrate the Garou as well as a number of Gifts that allows them to look like something else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-05T23:05:44-07:00","id":1485888,"title":"","content":"You can easily distinguish between wolves and coyotes. Coyotes are noticeably smaller and sound very different from wolves. At the very least, three out of the five breed forms should be giveaways. And I'm sure that beyond the visual and auditory clues humans can use, that senses like smell would make it even more noticeable.<br /> <br /> Unless there is a way to permanently alter or illusion the various forms, I don't think this is possible for anything other than a very short term con.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T02:42:20-07:00","id":1485896,"title":"","content":"You can't easily distinguish them in the game. In the 20th changing breed book, it specifically says werewolves can't tell the difference unless they have a lot of experience with the coyotes, which most probably never even seen one. It makes sense, since some bone gnawers are said to look sort of like dogs and metis can look all sort of weird. I will have to check the breed book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1926-lilitha","name":"Lilitha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T05:33:44-07:00","id":1485901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485886-nuwisha-pretending-to-be-a-werewolf?p=1485888#post1485888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can easily distinguish between wolves and coyotes. Coyotes are noticeably smaller and sound very different from wolves. At the very least, three out of the five breed forms should be giveaways. And I'm sure that beyond the visual and auditory clues humans can use, that senses like smell would make it even more noticeable.<br /> <br /> Unless there is a way to permanently alter or illusion the various forms, I don't think this is possible for anything other than a very short term con.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that there was a gift that did exact that. Made people believe you were just a Werewolf (not sure if it worked for other shifters). Don't got the Nuwisha book at hand, but will try and hunt it down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lilitha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485886-nuwisha-pretending-to-be-a-werewolf?p=1485896#post1485896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't easily distinguish them in the game. In the 20th changing breed book, it specifically says werewolves can't tell the difference unless they have a lot of experience with the coyotes, which most probably never even seen one. It makes sense, since some bone gnawers are said to look sort of like dogs and metis can look all sort of weird. I will have to check the breed book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure about that? Because if it says so, that's utterly stupid. You'd know the difference between a coyote and a wolf, letalone a beast with different perception of scent and hearing. Nuwisha are good, but Garou are not deaf and blind.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T08:20:15-07:00","id":1485906,"title":"","content":"Coyotes can be distinguished from wolves by how they invade urban areas and learn to not make noise and to use crosswalks to avoid being hit by cars. And no, I am not joking. Research has shown that they are very opportunistic and very circumspect about their traces.<br /> <br /> In terms of audiovisual and presumably scent ID, coyotes from the eastern US are probably more likely to be able to &quot;pass&quot; as wolves than those on the west, because of some interbreeding with wolves that went on with the eastern populations of coyotes. By anecdote, they also seem to be better fed when not eking out an existence in a literal desert (a neighbor lived in Cali for a while, said that all of the coyotes that he saw tended to be scraggly and mangy).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T11:51:47-07:00","id":1485925,"title":"","content":"I am aware of the differences between a wolf and coyote but here is what the book says: The Nuwisha are by far the most similar to the Garou of any of the Changing Breeds. Many Nuwisha use their physical resemblance to small, scrawny werewolves to pass themselves off as Garou....Only a werewolf who is exceedingly familiar with the Nuwisha can tell the difference without using supernatural means.<br /> <br /> I went through the breed book(there is only one version right?), but didn't really find anything about blending in with garou. Though the 20th changing breeds book does have a level 2 gift that apparently lets you look like any shifting race. So could even pass yourself off as a bird(though can't fly). There is also a level 5 gift that makes it so a group of people thinks you are a part of them, so you could trick a pack of werewolves into thinking you are in their pack(and it can work permanently). That is a bit too high level for my uses though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1926-lilitha","name":"Lilitha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T13:33:35-07:00","id":1485935,"title":"","content":"Bone Gnawer player here, you might be able to fool a bunch of non-Gnawers, but I just shared your Idea with the other Larpers and players of the Tribe here in the German part of the Barking Chain and I hope to be able to soon deliver a list of things that would make an imposter struggle amongst other Gnawers (and I am pretty sure at least one of them is turning this thought exercise into an exam for the Cliaths and Fosterns).<br /> I'll post more when I get the brainstorm back, but know that the first reactions were to tell you that the Nuwisha has better chances when faking Kinfolk. <br /> We had a Ratkin player successfully pose as Gnawer Kinfolk for almost half a year, because he in fact was the blood-related cousin of a Gnawer and there happened to be no Philodox (or Corax) available so noone happened to have the Scent of the True Form. It also helped that his cousin's Pack Totem Rat Spirit took a liking to this person, so noone felt the need to dig deeper.<br /> Even with this kind of head start it didn't last long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27469-ilsaena","name":"Ilsaena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T13:33:45-07:00","id":1485936,"title":"","content":"Personally, I would ignore that statement in the W20 Changing Breeds book. Anyone who sees a coyote in real life immediately knows it is not a wolf, even if it is the first time they ever see it. Coyotes have just as many fox-like features as wolf-like features. When the Lewis and Clark Expedition first saw a coyote they immediately knew it was neither a wolf or fox, but something different. They decided to refer to it as a &quot;prairie wolf&quot;, but don't let that designation fool you. They clearly knew it was not a gray wolf. Likewise when the Spanish first encountered it, they initially called it the Indian Fox before deciding adopting the Aztec word for it (coyotl) was better. Yet we wouldn't say that a Nuwisha looks like one of the Kitsune. Some people thought they look closer to jackals, but again not a jackal. So it's obvious people notice the similarity between a coyote and these other canids, but also clearly distinguish them as something else.<br /> <br /> The Crinos form is also sufficiently different. Nuwisha are around 7.5 to 8 feet, while Garou are roughly 9 feet (8-10). Nuwisha are around 250% of normal homid mass, while Garou are bewteen 400-850 lbs. Does that mean a Nuwisha could be mistaken for a small, scrawny werewolf? I would still say no because you would think a small, scrawny werewolf would also look small and scrawny in homid, and their homid form wouldn't. He'd look like a normal homid who just happens to have an extremely small and scrawny Crinos form which is not how this goes. And if you do have a Nuwisha who is a small and scrawny homid form, his Manabozho form would clearly not look enough like a Garou Crinos.<br /> <br /> It might have been possible that the first time European Garou met a Nuwisha they thought it was some kind of strange Garou (though the Three Brothers obviously knew they were not). But this isn't 500 years ago. The Nuwisha are known. Coyotes are known. A particularly ignorant and gullible Garou might not know any better, but most are going to know the Nuwisha is a Nuwisha, and his cover will be quickly blown. Certainly almost any Garou in North America will be able to identify him. Most Eurasian Garou will as well. Although it is always possible a particular sept of Bone Gnawers who are completely ignorant might not know that what they are seeing is a coyote and believe it is some strangely small wolf with many foxlike features (especially if he claimed to be Metis). But you are really stretching the gullibility of a small number of Garou here to do so, and I don't think that is what you want. <br /> <br /> And let's not forget, it would be super easy for any Garou who is even lightly suspicious to find someone with the Scent of True Form Gift who can immediately confirm that person is not Garou. Not to mention most spirits would likely already are able to distinguish the Changing Breeds from each other. Even one that may somehow be ignorant of the Nuwisha at minimum should recognize it is not a Garou or wolf IMO.<br /> <br /> So I think this would need a supernatural Gift to work independent of how a Nuwisha looks, sounds, smells. It seems like there may be such Gifts, but of course duration would be a critical factor. If it is something you cannot spam constantly, the Nuwisha would need to limit the amount of time spent among the Garou, and that could become suspicious in itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T13:42:13-07:00","id":1485939,"title":"","content":"Coyotes are obviously different from wolves. But so are jackals, dogs and all other things that pass as Garou. It seems plausible that the Garou would accept the ruse not because of not noticing the newcomer isn't an actual wolf, but because they need to know enough about coyotes in general and also the Nuwisha in particular to notice that this particular &quot;wolfy&quot; thing can't be a Garou at all.<br /> <br /> Any Garou that knows how to distinguish coyotes from wolves, but also heard about Silent Striders and Bunyip, has no reason to not fall for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T14:45:43-07:00","id":1485941,"title":"","content":"That is actually a good point, silent striders are jackals, and the bunyip are thylacine(which definitely don't look like wolves), plus you have some of the bone gnawers are described as large dogs. So there really is a large variety of what a garou might look like. With that in mind, it does make me think that pretending to be a silent strider might be easier. A coyote is probably easier to mistake for a jackal than a wolf, and you would have a built in reason for going off on your own to do stuff. They are also not as well known. That gives a little more distance from the other wolves, to help pull off the trick.<br /> <br /> I do agree spirits would likely know, but I don't think they would care. They are treated like ragabash garou for learning gifts and it is mentioned luna sees them as such. I feel most spirits would just go along with that and not care too much. And even if a spirit does care, it isn't likely to flat out tell people.<br /> <br /> Scent of the true form is something I have considered and it is one of my biggest concerns. I feel like while most garou probably don't use it on each other randomly, it is definitely a threat. There is a level 3 gift that allows you to hide your scent and it specifically says it works on scent of true form, in that it raises the difficulty roll by the number of successes. However that is a bit high ranking for the character in mind, and also even with an increased difficulty, they would only need 2 successes on the roll. This is more questionable, but I wonder if you could pass scent of true form by using scent of running water. Since it is based off scent, and you wouldn't have a scent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1926-lilitha","name":"Lilitha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T15:04:48-07:00","id":1485943,"title":"","content":"Yeah, resembling a child of Owl is definitely something you want to avoid amongst the children of Rat.<br /> <br /> Also the random, unprovoked usage of detection Gifts is something that might be rarer in other Tribes, but living between Weaver Boulevard and Wyrm Avenue means that Gnawers tend to be exactly where the THINGS are who disguise themselves as humans... well, if you think of it, they're ones themselves. <br /> In short, noone is more likely to stumble upon supernaturals who can assume homid guises than urban Garou, so your infiltration strategy can't rely on the hope that none of them will turn out to be paranoid enough to randomly sniff for the true form of people.<br /> <br /> Also faking to be a Metis would be especially tricky with Gnawers because they are most likely to know some Metis intimately enough to know the small telltale signs: Silver should burn you in Homid, you should regenerate in Homid and don't Metis shift back to Crinos as soon as they fall asleep?<br /> <br /> Oh and I don't know if that's something official, but our Corax have SIGHT of the True Form because Corax have that poor sense of smell thing going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27469,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27469-ilsaena","user":"Ilsaena","date":". 07-06-2022, 06:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27469-ilsaena","name":"Ilsaena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T15:15:37-07:00","id":1485944,"title":"","content":"Is there a way to get around scent of true form though, one that doesn't require already being a very high rank?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1926-lilitha","name":"Lilitha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T16:10:41-07:00","id":1485945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lilitha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485886-nuwisha-pretending-to-be-a-werewolf?p=1485941#post1485941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is actually a good point, silent striders are jackals...</div> </div> </div> </div>Most likely the golden jackal, aka an actual wolf aka the African wolf. They wouldn't be able to get with other jackals without the help of the Mokole; jackals are about as far away from wolves as African wild painted dogs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T16:52:33-07:00","id":1485946,"title":"","content":"I believe the golden jackals are mentioned as options for silent striders, but the pure breed ones are described as the sleek black ones from Egyptian art. Which I think are just Pharaoh Hound, which are straight up dogs. Apparently there are some red talons that are African wild dogs too. It is a fantasy game, so not everything needs to translate or make sense in real life terms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1926-lilitha","name":"Lilitha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T17:02:39-07:00","id":1485947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lilitha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485886-nuwisha-pretending-to-be-a-werewolf?p=1485946#post1485946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe the golden jackals are mentioned as options for silent striders, but the pure breed ones are described as the sleek black ones from Egyptian art. Which I think are just Pharaoh Hound, which are straight up dogs. Apparently there are some red talons that are African wild dogs too. It is a fantasy game, so not everything needs to translate or make sense in real life terms.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Kucha Ekundu, Cape Hunting Dog Red Talons are only viable because, like the Bunyip, they underwent the Mokole rite that allows shifting Varna from one animal to another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T17:17:40-07:00","id":1485948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lilitha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485886-nuwisha-pretending-to-be-a-werewolf?p=1485941#post1485941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With that in mind, it does make me think that pretending to be a silent strider might be easier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep it simple. Trying to pass for a jackal is harder than just being an unspecified canidae. And there's enough crossbreeding between tribes that you can pass for any tribe that's easier for your ruse than hyper-focus on a single option.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lilitha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485886-nuwisha-pretending-to-be-a-werewolf?p=1485941#post1485941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is more questionable, but I wonder if you could pass scent of true form by using scent of running water. Since it is based off scent, and you wouldn't have a scent.</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> Scent of Running Water isn't meant to hide information from supernatural powers of detection and you already cited a gift meant specifically for this that is Rank 3. This is the kind of thing that changes completely the role of a key Gift in the game and have many other repercussions.<br /> <br /> Better to develop a Gift specifically for your intent. It may be Nuwisha, Rank 1, and make SoTF require 5 successes to get you, identifying you as Garou with 2 to 4 successes. It may cost Gnosis to activate for a number of days or something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-06T17:34:16-07:00","id":1485949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485886-nuwisha-pretending-to-be-a-werewolf?p=1485947#post1485947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Kucha Ekundu, Cape Hunting Dog Red Talons are only viable because, like the Bunyip, they underwent the Mokole rite that allows shifting Varna from one animal to another.</div> </div> </div> </div>How hard it is to use another animal isn't the problem because the goal isn't to fool the greatest sages among the Garou, it is to fool a small group.<br /> <br /> Most Garou have little knowledge about the Nuwisha beyond having heard of them, exceedingly few know what it takes to breed with similar animals compared with how many have heard of this happening. Even biologists don't simply know every animal on Earth from memory to recognize a Golden Jackal and argue about the Silent Striders at length.<br /> <br /> All those information are relevant and exist in the setting, but most characters won't have them at hand or reason to think of this possibility. It's easy when we're examining from the point where we already know that the character is a Nuwisha trying to pass for Garou, but for the actual in game characters it would probably take something happening to make them really put the effort into figuring out that the weird wolf is actually a Nuwisha, specifically, and not only just a weird wolf form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-07T01:17:24-07:00","id":1485967,"title":"","content":"So the Gnawer Bashs have brainstormed<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> A thing that came up here is that a randomly activated Scent of the True Form (with On Patrol thrown in for good measure) is only among the third most likely things that could make a Nuwisha imposter stumble.<br /> <br /> You'd have to also have a plan for Truth of Gaia. And yes, Gnawer players are randomly &quot;truthed&quot; a lot. A LOT.<br /> I can't remember if it ever happened to me during introduction while stating my Tribe (or Rank or Name or Auspice or Breed), but from what I hear of other players this is something that happens frequently when entering someone else's territory and anyone on guard duty has access to the Gift (which is a Cliath Gift so good luck).<br /> <br /> Next there is the thing that Gnawers most likely have the most Cliath Gifts from any Tribe in the game (I can't be bothered to fact check this so I'm not adamant about them being number one, but they have a lot of Tribe-only Gifts on Cliath). There's something specialized to make your life easier for any kind of personality. Not knowing a single one of those and 'only having Resist Toxin' is raising suspicion the higher the Rank you try to pose as.<br /> <br /> Then there is the thing that quite a number of Gnawer Gifts, especially the information trading ones, deliberately target Gnawers. So not being able to understand the Barking Chain or orders masked by Rant and Rave would likely come up as a problem sooner than a randomly activated Scent of the True Form, too. Also you wouldn't be able to be targeted by Friend in Need, but if THAT'S what is blowing your disguise, you're having different problems anyway<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And the most likely thing an imposter would stumble over:<br /> Never having heard of the Gnawer currency system of shit, junk, stuff and loot and the exchange rates from one category to another and how the currency of information is handled therein.<br /> <br /> Further honorable mentions of things that maybe are not suspicious per se, but add up:<br /> Never having heard of the Ban of Man.<br /> Not knowing a lot about human homeless culture, drugs, cops, how begging works, the legal system including the inner workings of a jail, violent subcultures and punk music.<br /> Not knowing any of the low-level survivability Rites of the Tribe like Shopping Cart or Cardboard Palace.<br /> Never having heard of the different Camps and weird Gnawer Totems.<br /> Having the resources Background at all (or a job or a home or too much money in your pocket) and being targeted by the Gift Smell of Success (because one of the Gnawers WILL check the 'new guy' out).<br /> Not having any untraditional/unhonorable things dedicated to yourself that just make sense to have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27469-ilsaena","name":"Ilsaena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-07T01:27:05-07:00","id":1485970,"title":"","content":"Ilsaena, one would think there's a whole academy teaching Bone Gnawers how to be Bone Gnawers with harsh exams and diplomas the way you put it.<br /> It's less about how paranoid and a closed social group they are and more about &quot;how to facilitate Nuwisha's narrative roles as infiltrators and educators&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-07T01:31:33-07:00","id":1485971,"title":"","content":"I'm just answering the original question &quot;What are some things that might give you away&quot; (when impersonating a Garou and choosing to say you're a Gnawer Bash of all things) in the form of a buffet for a Storyteller to choose from problems that a Nuwisha might run into when trying to go &quot;really deep&quot;. Not trying to make a point here that it's impossible to superficially fool a few Garou for a while. And I'm also not trying to make a point on how extremely professionally secretive and paranoid Gnawers are. Most of those challenges occur when individuals with the Gnawer skillset and Gift-set feel curious, greedy, silly or bored.<br /> <br /> If you ask the information gathering Tribe to dig deep, you unsurprisingly get a stash of intel <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27469,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27469-ilsaena","user":"Ilsaena","date":". 07-07-2022, 04:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27469-ilsaena","name":"Ilsaena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-07T02:35:45-07:00","id":1485972,"title":"","content":"I'd just like to note that, yes,coyotes and wolves look different. But coyotes and wolves can interbreed and coywolves are fairly common in the US.<br /> <br /> And since we do not have a canon description of where coywolves go, having a coywolf pretend to be garou makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-07T03:47:29-07:00","id":1485974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485886-nuwisha-pretending-to-be-a-werewolf?p=1485949#post1485949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How hard it is to use another animal isn't the problem because the goal isn't to fool the greatest sages among the Garou, it is to fool a small group.<br /> <br /> Most Garou have little knowledge about the Nuwisha beyond having heard of them, exceedingly few know what it takes to breed with similar animals compared with how many have heard of this happening. Even biologists don't simply know every animal on Earth from memory to recognize a Golden Jackal and argue about the Silent Striders at length.<br /> <br /> All those information are relevant and exist in the setting, but most characters won't have them at hand or reason to think of this possibility. It's easy when we're examining from the point where we already know that the character is a Nuwisha trying to pass for Garou, but for the actual in game characters it would probably take something happening to make them really put the effort into figuring out that the weird wolf is actually a Nuwisha, specifically, and not only just a weird wolf form.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Um....yes. Did you mean to quote me or someone else? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-07T06:40:30-07:00","id":1485980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ilsaena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485886-nuwisha-pretending-to-be-a-werewolf?p=1485971#post1485971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you ask the information gathering Tribe to dig deep, you unsurprisingly get a stash of intel <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interestin view of the Gnawers, I've always seen them as the survivor tribe. There are some &quot;oh people don't notice the sad, lonely and broken, so we learn things&quot; vibe as well, but their chief quality and capability is their resilience and the way they adapted to surviving and thriving in the gutters of humanity.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-07T08:20:03-07:00","id":1485986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485886-nuwisha-pretending-to-be-a-werewolf?p=1485980#post1485980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's an interestin view of the Gnawers, I've always seen them as the survivor tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>And how would that make them easier to infiltrate?<br /> <br /> Anyway, Tribes are allowed to have more than one layer and two different things can be true at the same time.<br /> Being able to put an ear to the pavewalk and let 'Streets tell Stories' while half the Tribe can turn invisible is simultaneously spying and survival. Maybe you didn't read my earlier ramblings but I was trying to make the point that being a decent spy or detective is directly affecting your survivability when you're in the Wyrms back yard and the Weavers home ground.<br /> Thus making 'simply' faking a Gnawer Bash a surprising challenge for a Nuwisha (or a Hunter, Mage, obfuscating Vampire, Clone, Alien, Bigfoot or simply a Ronin who tries to blend in and pick up Gifts because everyone thinks Gnawers are easy to fake)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27469,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27469-ilsaena","user":"Ilsaena","date":". 07-07-2022, 11:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27469-ilsaena","name":"Ilsaena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-07T10:11:15-07:00","id":1485988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485886-nuwisha-pretending-to-be-a-werewolf?p=1485974#post1485974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Um....yes. Did you mean to quote me or someone else? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You, but the post wasn't exclusively for you, at most the very first short paragraph.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ilsaena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485886-nuwisha-pretending-to-be-a-werewolf?p=1485971#post1485971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just answering the original question &quot;What are some things that might give you away&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>There are three problems in general with your post, and keep in mind that they have more to do with what it seemed to imply than what you personally intended, I get we may have had a miscommunication here anyway.<br /> <br /> First, not every Gnawer is a perfect example of a Gnawer, much less knows everything about the tribe. You're a clueless cub before you are deep in the ways of the tribe and personal upbringing and area have a lot to say on what you're really capable of knowing or doing at first. This is specially relevant for the Gnawer currency and the Ban of Man, unless the impostor is trying to pass as a seasoned tribe member he would be ridiculed for the ignorance before being strongly suspect of deception, and then would just learn about them in the same way as the Gnawers.<br /> <br /> Second, trying to infiltrate any specific tribe as one of them is tricky and doesn't seems to be the goal. The idea is to infiltrate a more cosmopolitan Caern by pretending to be of a Tribe that isn't particularly common there. And then no one would be knowledgeable about the specific ways of the tribe. Trying to fool the tribe itself isn't a smart prospect for a Rank 1 or 2 Nuwisha anyway.<br /> <br /> And third, you're assuming the impostor won't know nothing about the ways of the target, and that's ignoring the whole shtick of the Nuwisha. They're more likely to know about all those things than anyone other than a Gnawer, period, and an infiltrator would probably study about them with some other Nuwisha or their repositories of lore stolen from other Changers. Seriously, they're so good with it that some Breed and Tribe Books are written in universe <i>by</i> the Nuwisha (usually Old Man Manyskins).<br /> <br /> Nuwisha have several advantages to disguise as Garou, the first being to treat Ragabash Gifts as Breed Gifts, period (a specific trick from Coyote that makes for a blanket declaration that they all count as Garou Ragabash for learning Gifts), their forms other than Manabozho can easily pass as the corresponding forms of the Garou (the Manabozho would stand out more, but not be impossible to explain), and the sheer rarity of the Nuwisha makes for the suspicion that they're what they really are very unlikely.<br /> <br /> If the proper Gifts are taken, all this talk is moot. Up to level 2 the Nuwisha already have access to the means to imitate any Changer on a broad enough spectrum of things as to just need a few lies to justify the rest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-07T10:29:02-07:00","id":1485991,"title":"","content":"And how is any of that a problem or three ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27469-ilsaena","name":"Ilsaena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-07T11:01:08-07:00","id":1485995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ilsaena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485886-nuwisha-pretending-to-be-a-werewolf?p=1485991#post1485991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And how is any of that a problem or three ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Miscommunication, I said it right in the first paragraph.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-07T11:04:24-07:00","id":1485996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lilitha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485886-nuwisha-pretending-to-be-a-werewolf?p=1485941#post1485941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do agree spirits would likely know, but I don't think they would care.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe not any random spirit, but packs have their pack totems, and septs have their caern totems. Those spirits have an incentive to notify their children (the Garou members of the pack, or the leadership or general members of the sept who perform the Moot Rite) about what is really going on. Now depending on the nature of those spirits, certain ones may choose not to mention it. Trickster spirits or Coyote as pack totem may withhold that information until the &quot;right&quot; time. But I think most spirits would inform their children, and certain spirits probably act as killjoys regardless (likely many Totems of Respect).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-07T13:49:05-07:00","id":1486008,"title":"","content":"I don't think a lot of the bone gnawer stuff is that big of an issue, since there is no reason you couldn't have a zero resource Nuwisha who has lived on the street at some point. In fact one of their totems, Raven, has the ban that they can't carry any wealth on their person. The other points do bring up some issues.<br /> <br /> The gift thing is an issue longer term, though nuwisha do get access to one bone gnawer gift(it actually seems like they get access to one gift from almost all of the tribes). Which is scent of sweet honey. It has one benefit, in that you could use it in front of everyone at the time of your choosing and make it known you have a gnawer gift. I believe it is a tribe only gift, so pulling that out early on should keep any doubts away. For rituals, you could probably get the garou themselves to teach them to you.<br /> <br /> Truth of gaia is an issue of course. Though I think there are ways around that with clever word play. You could say something like, &quot;I am Laughing Moon, trickster of Luna, friend of rat, born as human.&quot; That could be your actual rite name(none of the garou are going to know a low level nuwisha rite name). You are a trickster of luna, and you could have a pet rat, named rat. Everything you say would be true and truth of gaia would confirm it. At that point you would be pretty much in right?<br /> <br /> I am not really sure what to do about stuff like rant and rave, or barking chain. I suppose for barking chain you could say you were too far away, though rant and raves specifically targets you. At that point, I am not sure what would happen. They probably wouldn't pick you out as Nuwisha, but assume you lied about your tribe, which if you are a ragabash might fit. Though I imagine they would be pissed. I am not sure claiming you were in another tribe after that, and hanging with them would be an option at that point without a massive amount of scrutiny.<br /> <br /> I am still not sure what to do about scent of true form, other than the one gift that makes it slightly harder but requires you being high rank.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1926-lilitha","name":"Lilitha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-07T14:43:45-07:00","id":1486011,"title":"","content":"Yeah, now we're talking. With actual knowledge about street life and a talent for acting you can go places.<br /> <br /> Using the Scent of Sweet Honey in front of Gnawer witnesses early on would help you out a lot. If you use it in a creative way, so that your story will be told for you, you've opened an idiosyncrasy credit you can work with, for example when you use that Gift to lure insects to a corpse to mess with the forensics of human law enforcement. Gnawers will tell your story and have a laugh and you're golden as far as first impressions go.<br /> <br /> Your way to introduce yourself wouldn't fly far with how we play it. You see, as much as all Gets are considered almost an Ahroun honoris causa, most Gnawers are versed in being Bashy. So planning and fantasizing about how you could work around Truth of Gaia yourself makes you sensitive for verbal acrobatics. And messing with the wording of your introduction is something we know from Stargazers and Ronin where I come from. So your Nuwisha would have to work around how exactly the players of your area choose to play the Howl of introduction. It's not impossible, but not trivial either.<br /> With enough clever Intel you might be able to just state a Camp, if you're really that good. That would work around not stating 'I am a Gnawer' because as far as anyone knows 'I am a Frankweiler' is everything you need to say to become one if we're being picky to trick the Gift. But as I said, that means you'd need to witness the Garou introduce themselves to each other to work out a strategy beforehand. (And no that's not impossible when the coyote can turn invisible anyway). And yes, pulling that off in a way that fits how your troupe plays introductions would bring you 'pretty much in'.<br /> <br /> I think that if suspicion is raised, it won't go immediately in the direction of you not being a wolf, it is much more likely that the initial suspicion would be that you're simply a Ronin who lied about his past trying to scam Gnawers to learn survival Rites and Gifts. <br /> Depending on how useful and funny you have been to the Gnawers you might fake being that Ronin and maybe even a simple 'please don't ask, I mean you guys only the best' could work towards staying even a little longer.<br /> In fact, I think faking a Ronin who refuses to talk about the Name and Tribe he doesn't have anymore might be possible to pull of, if you just really made them like you beforehand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27469-ilsaena","name":"Ilsaena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-07T19:22:21-07:00","id":1486020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485886-nuwisha-pretending-to-be-a-werewolf?p=1485996#post1485996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe not any random spirit, but packs have their pack totems, and septs have their caern totems. Those spirits have an incentive to notify their children (the Garou members of the pack, or the leadership or general members of the sept who perform the Moot Rite) about what is really going on. Now depending on the nature of those spirits, certain ones may choose not to mention it. Trickster spirits or Coyote as pack totem may withhold that information until the &quot;right&quot; time. But I think most spirits would inform their children, and certain spirits probably act as killjoys regardless (likely many Totems of Respect).</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the very description of the Nuwisha, I disagree. First because I don't think those spirits have a close enough relationship with the Garou to just go about telling this (even Pack Totems are more like minor gods than familiars trope-wise), but mostly because this is the lore directly saying that the Nuwisha can and do pull this out with some frequency and most Garou never find out, so applying this rationale would render unfeasible a kind of story that canonically happens.<br /> <br /> One way around this is to consider that the Nuwisha are still allies and seen as such by the spirits. They make fools of the Garou, but also help with their fight and teach lessons that generally further the spirit's agenda instead of hindering it. Another way is to consider that blank statement about being seen as Ragabash as literal and the spirit not being able to tell the difference.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lilitha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485886-nuwisha-pretending-to-be-a-werewolf?p=1486008#post1486008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am still not sure what to do about scent of true form, other than the one gift that makes it slightly harder but requires you being high rank.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bribe the Gift user.<br /> <br /> Like, seriously, if it comes to that, just let them in the joke. You're not a Wyrmling, for Gaia's sake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-07T19:54:35-07:00","id":1486021,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of trying to pass yourself off as a Ronin if caught, as a backup plan. Because if that 'catch' you, they will probably be confident in thinking they figure it all out so wouldn't consider that you are actually not a garou at all.<br /> <br /> I also like the idea of trying to bribe them. Because if someone has scent of true form, it is more than likely going to be a philodox. Which you wouldn't think would be easy to bribe, but it also means they are the ones most likely to respect your role given by gaia. I wouldn't say it is easy, but it would make for an interesting roleplay interaction. Which, if it is interesting enough, also might help you win the player over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1926-lilitha","name":"Lilitha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-08T02:08:27-07:00","id":1486032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ilsaena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485886-nuwisha-pretending-to-be-a-werewolf?p=1485986#post1485986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And how would that make them easier to infiltrate?</div> </div> </div> </div>I said nothing there about infiltration, was just confused by the focus of spies of the streets that you have for them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-08T02:16:39-07:00","id":1486034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485886-nuwisha-pretending-to-be-a-werewolf?p=1485996#post1485996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe not any random spirit, but packs have their pack totems, and septs have their caern totems. Those spirits have an incentive to notify their children (the Garou members of the pack, or the leadership or general members of the sept who perform the Moot Rite) about what is really going on. Now depending on the nature of those spirits, certain ones may choose not to mention it. Trickster spirits or Coyote as pack totem may withhold that information until the &quot;right&quot; time. But I think most spirits would inform their children, and certain spirits probably act as killjoys regardless (likely many Totems of Respect).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm this is an interesting question and one that wasn't included in the breed book. I wonder if it may be that the Nuwisha have some kind of a standing deal with such spirits? &quot;You don't notice us because we have to be here to do our job, capisce?&quot; This of course would make for a quite awesome clusterfuck if there was a corrupted Nuwisha using the same deals and blind spots to fuck a Sept up.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-08T04:20:02-07:00","id":1486035,"title":"","content":"I think that one could argue that the breed books weren't written with every detail of every other book in mind. They tell their own story with their own theme, and with the Nuwisha book you can even get a different feel from the illustrations.<br /> <br /> It's like with making Umbra crossovers work: sometimes you have to decide whether you're telling a Mage story or a Werewolf story to decide how a certain aspect &quot;really&quot; unfolds.<br /> <br /> In a Nuwisha-centered story one could argue that of course those ultimate Tricksters got a deal worked out with the 'truthful' spirits ages ago and even the most honorbound entities of pure honesty somehow managed to at least stay silent out of respect for the Nuwishas role.<br /> <br /> The same question can be equally well answered the other way around when the focus of your story lies elsewhere. Then those pesky coyotes (who have no honor but humor instead) are just one of the many reasons why those honesty-bound spirits are adamant in their ways in the first place.<br /> <br /> If you exaggerate in both directions you'll see that the answer neither can be that no Nuwisha ever manages to come near a Caern with a Totem of Respect, nor can it be that there is an ancient deal for a free pass for all Nuwisha ever, because, like Asmodai said, in the history of the world there would have come up at least one 'awesome clusterfuck' because leaving such a back door open can't go well indefinitely.<br /> <br /> That's why I like to brainstorm possible complications and have a look on how the arsenals and tool boxes of the different sides interact with each other to get a feeling on how this game of hide-and-seek could play out.<br /> <br /> I am a fan of the Idea of some kind of standing deal, but I would argue that this deal wouldn't be worded in a way that lets the Trickster off the hook completely. <br /> As a powerful Totem Spirit of honor and honesty I might be able to sense the nature of every visitor to my Caern and I might be able to accept that Gaia gave that Werecoyote the job of tricking my allies/servants into learning a lesson and I might see how me seeing right through the charade would hinder Gaia's plan for that Trickster so I might take him to the side and tell him that his secret is safe with me.<br /> But I might also tell him that Gaia made it his job to stay sharp and be smart about it and that Gaia didn't give me my watchful Spirit eyes just to look away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27469-ilsaena","name":"Ilsaena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-08T06:24:59-07:00","id":1486036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ilsaena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485886-nuwisha-pretending-to-be-a-werewolf?p=1486035#post1486035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that one could argue that the breed books weren't written with every detail of every other book in mind. They tell their own story with their own theme...</div> </div> </div> </div>You wouldn't even have to argue, it's a fact. They were written by different people in different times and contexts without a clear singular definition of how every interaction we can think of would work in the setting. White Wolf never bothered being consistant. That allowed them to do all kinds of crazy shit and be really inspired, but if you believe everything written is the absolute truth you're gonna be in a world of pain.<br /> <br /> This is just within a single line. Now add in the other lines that really don't play well with each other and the poor saps who believe there is an absolute truth of a hollistic WOD and you're in all the pain ever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-08T11:28:51-07:00","id":1486051,"title":"","content":"Most of the Nuwisha live in the umbra permanently, so you would think that they do have really strong connection with the spirits. So the idea that they made deals with spirits seem pretty reasonable. All Nuwisha can learn spirit speech at rank one. So step one might include talking to local spirits and making deals prior to meeting any of the garou.<br /> <br /> In fact, the more I think about it, the more I think that the scouting phase is key. Instead of just starting scene one, showing up and meeting garou, might need to do some scouting out of local customs, meet the local spirits and make deals and stuff like that. It might be possible to convince a vulture spirit to block scent of true form one time, or get some sneaky spirit to help you evade it. Making a deal with a dog spirit to inform you of what is said in a barking chain would also be possible. Actually, if you get a dog spirit to tell you what is said with barking chain, that might be a good way to gather information ahead of time as you can spy on what they are saying to each other(or if they are not using it at all then that it useful information too).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1926-lilitha","name":"Lilitha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-08T12:28:24-07:00","id":1486058,"title":"","content":"I would say the main reason a Nuwisha &quot;infiltration&quot; would work is the whole Garou mentality and history<br /> The Garou are basically a cult with heavy brainwashing/conditioning<br /> A bunch of teens, kids after the First change are tossed in to a bootcamp to be &quot;educated&quot;, learn the Garou version of the stories and preapre for their sometimes deadly rite of passage to be warriors ready to die for gaia<br /> And the Sprits KNOW the Garou are mass murdered other Fera, disturbed the fragile balance and remained as arrogant as they were in the past ~7-10k years....<br /> And they never forget... nor forgive<br /> Just think about it!<br /> The Chosen Race, Warriors of Gia who - in theory - would need every bit of help to drag back the world from the edge of Apocalypse are have to BEG basically to the Spritis for help, to teach them morsels of power, Gifts and the Spirits - more often than not - ask a heavy price, services, spirit quest and all you can think of from &quot;from now you have to feed any stray dog you encounter&quot; to outright suicide missions<br /> I highly doubt there are spirits who genuinely respect or &quot;love&quot; the Garou, in my humble oppinion, they tolerate them at best<br /> The only thing in the books that is constant is the fact the spirits will never help a Garou for free. You can't find a supplement where in an example story, or description you find a spirit who rushed to help to a young cub &quot;Hey kid, wanna learn a cool power? I know you will need to save Gaia!&quot; Sure Caerns and pack totems help... but even they ask a price.<br /> A Nuwisha shows up near a pack &quot;Guys, Im a Ragabash, a bit scrawny, only survivor or my pack mind if I'm tag along? would totally fly - the spirits actually know, the Nuwisha are good guys, better than the Garou actually, and they still do their job... would sooner help a Nuwisha then a bunch of moron wolves<br /> At least in my humble opinion<br /> Garou education is horrible, with a shaky relationship with humanity<br /> A Garou near New york probably never even seen a live Coyote, maybe only in the zoo... looks like kinda of a wolf.<br /> As Lilitha said, a little leg work, a little background check and preparation... fooling a Pack is easy, heck, a pro could even show up in a moot and probaby no one would suspect anything","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-08T12:51:34-07:00","id":1486061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485886-nuwisha-pretending-to-be-a-werewolf?p=1486058#post1486058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say the main reason a Nuwisha &quot;infiltration&quot; would work is the whole Garou mentality and history<br /> The Garou are basically a cult with heavy brainwashing/conditioning<br /> A bunch of teens,</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, the Garou would love if they had large groups of younger newcomers. Usually, though, it's one or two cubs, and they might be from less impressionable walks of life and stages of existence. Some weren't even human to begin with and just experienced a lightning-fast revelation about deception and language use to fit in with humans, and as adult wolves, aren't really necessarily keen on just going along with everything (territory, expanded as a concept, demands some kind of challenge).<br /> <br /> You can have Garou Academy, but it's not the default assumption of the setting. Miles away from it, really. They're a limited and dying resistance fighting an asymmetric war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-08T22:50:10-07:00","id":1486083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485886-nuwisha-pretending-to-be-a-werewolf?p=1486058#post1486058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">; <br /> ...fooling a Pack is easy, heck, a pro could even show up in a moot and probaby no one would suspect anything</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree with every point you make, I take it you have never Larped a WoD System?<br /> <br /> Theory crafting at the table or in a forum is easy, one, maybe five smart heads have a talk and come up with how it 'probably would unfold', finding a likely course of action. Coming to the conclusion, that a pro con man should be able to just do things.<br /> <br /> But when you actually are confronted with 20, 40, sometimes 60 different people at an Elysium/Caern/whatever, it is just flabbergasting how many personalities out there just think SO differently than you might think that a sensible person would think.<br /> There are so many factors that can turn out to be sheer 'bad luck': someone just got promoted into the guardian team and want to impress the Warder, someone just learned a new detection Gift and is excited to have any excuse to try it out, someone takes a liking to your character just because your nose looks sexy and you end up with the annoying kind of attention, someone has had a weird upbringing and behaves in a way which you would think that 'noone would be this stupid', someone tries to impress his Shadow Lord Alpha and is randomly trying to dig up dirt about visitors... <br /> Often you're amazed with how bad the security turns out to be, but equally often you get the random unprovoked scrutiny of someone bored or curious or ambitious for all the wrong reasons.<br /> <br /> Also, for secluded brain-wash-cults visitors are a main source of entertainment and as a visitor you're often pushed into far more story telling than you're actually able to spend time listening in.<br /> <br /> So yeah, a pro could pull it of to just show up at a moot, but the 'noone would suspect anything' part is a gamble I'd be very paranoid about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27469-ilsaena","name":"Ilsaena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-09T08:06:52-07:00","id":1486097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ilsaena</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1485886-nuwisha-pretending-to-be-a-werewolf?p=1486083#post1486083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I agree with every point you make, I take it you have never Larped a WoD System?</div> </div> </div> </div>And you're the first one to even mention a LARP here. I'm not sure if any Sept would even have 40+ members.<br /> <br /> LARPs have a distinct dynamic that changes everything for a lot of reasons. For example, while all those kinds of people exist as NPCs too, in a TT game you can just avoid them, because you're not physically constrained as a player to be regularly in line of sight of other people. In LARPs everyone is a PC, you have to consider their behavior as such (for example, probably 95% knows the Nuwisha, <b>and 80% or more read their own Tribe Books</b>), and so many factors change drastically.<br /> <br /> Things that work fine for one mode of play are plain stupid in the other, which is why sometimes key aspects of the setting must change or be reconsidered under a whole new light. This isn't to say that your considerations don't hold some water, but that assuming that the LARP dynamics should inform the general question is silly and not really helpful for others in a vacuum.<br /> <br /> We would need a whole new discussion (here or elsewhere) to talk about the infiltration trope in LARPs altogether. Which is a valid topic, just not what was being discussed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-09T14:31:53-07:00","id":1486114,"title":"","content":"No. The Storyteller is just not able to portray a Sept of 6 Packs (30) plus wandering Guests (10) in the way they would behave if they were portrayed by 40 players. Maybe you can avoid this at your table because the table ignores the fact that every person out there feels they are the main character of their own story, which is how individuals behave. So bringing up examples of what can randomly happen if everyone behaves like a person instead of being a NPC who only jumps in and out of existence when the Storyteller remembers to use them is a well-meaning hint what to keep in mind when portraying a &quot;pro infiltrator&quot;.<br /> Of course you could argue that point is invalid as well if you play the way that you don't need to think about the portrayal of unusual skills. I for my part enjoy brainstorming with as many smart people as possible when I plan on portraying any kind of skill at a &quot;pro&quot; level.<br /> So I hope the people who plan to portray a Nuwisha use those tidbits to entertain their table and show off how well their characters have thought about everything even if this means they're 'unnecessarily' prepared for problems that wouldn't come up at their table because their ST is only human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27469-ilsaena","name":"Ilsaena","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-09T15:07:05-07:00","id":1486116,"title":"","content":"I think it is good to consider every situation, even stuff like having 40 different people at a LARP. Because you never really know how other players are going to react, and there might be only a 1 in 40 chance a player is going to do something, but what happens if that person happens to be the one at the table? It might just be bad luck but you still have to deal with. Ultimately I am not sure if a big group helps or hinders the chance of sneaking into a sept. On one hand there is a lot more people who might notice something, but on the other hand you are likely to get less attention directed specifically at you. So there are benefits and downsides.<br /> <br /> I feel like, to be confident with the plan, I need to sort of expect everything will happen. That at some point someone will use scent of true form and stuff on me, and it is more a matter of when than if. So need to consider all those possibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1926-lilitha","name":"Lilitha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},